rface":"பத்து","parts":[{"text":"பத்து","lemma":"pattu","gloss":"ten"}],"gloss":"ten"},{"surface":"ஈனும்மோ","parts":[{"text":"ஈனும்","lemma":"īṉum","gloss":"will give birth"},{"text":"ஓ","lemma":"ō","gloss":"interrogative particle"}],"gloss":"does it give birth?"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"நின்னும்","parts":[{"text":"நின்","lemma":"niṉ","gloss":"you"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"um","gloss":"and"}],"gloss":"you too"},{"surface":"நின்","parts":[{"text":"நின்","lemma":"niṉ","gloss":"your"}],"gloss":"your"},{"surface":"மலையும்","parts":[{"text":"மலை","lemma":"malai","gloss":"mountain"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"um","gloss":"and"}],"gloss":"mountain too"},{"surface":"பாடி","parts":[{"text":"பாடு","lemma":"pāṭu","gloss":"sing"},{"text":"இ","lemma":"i","gloss":"having"}],"gloss":"having sung"},{"surface":"வருநர்க்கு","parts":[{"text":"வருநர்","lemma":"varunar","gloss":"those who come"},{"text":"கு","lemma":"ku","gloss":"to"}],"gloss":"to those who come"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"இன்முகம்","parts":[{"text":"இன்முகம்","lemma":"இன்முகம்","gloss":"pleasant face"}],"gloss":"pleasant face","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"கரவாது","parts":[{"text":"கர","lemma":"kara","gloss":"hide"},{"text":"ஆது","lemma":"ātu","gloss":"without"}],"gloss":"without hiding"},{"surface":"உவந்து","parts":[{"text":"உவந்து","lemma":"உவந்து","gloss":"rejoicing"}],"gloss":"rejoicing","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"நீ","parts":[{"text":"நீ","lemma":"nī","gloss":"you"}],"gloss":"you"},{"surface":"அளித்த","parts":[{"text":"அளி","lemma":"aḷi","gloss":"give"},{"text":"த்த","lemma":"tta","gloss":"past relative participle"}],"gloss":"that you gifted"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"அண்ணல்","parts":[{"text":"அண்ணல்","lemma":"aṇṇal","gloss":"majestic"}],"gloss":"majestic"},{"surface":"யானை","parts":[{"text":"யானை","lemma":"yāṉai","gloss":"elephant"}],"gloss":"elephant"},{"surface":"எண்ணின்","parts":[{"text":"எண்","lemma":"eṇ","gloss":"count"},{"text":"இன்","lemma":"iṉ","gloss":"if"}],"gloss":"if counted"},{"surface":"கொங்கர்","parts":[{"text":"கொங்கர்","lemma":"koṅkar","gloss":"Kongu people"}],"gloss":"of the Kongu warriors"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"குடகடல்","parts":[{"text":"குடகடல்","lemma":"குடகடல்","gloss":"western sea"}],"gloss":"western sea","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"ஓட்டிய","parts":[{"text":"ஓட்டு","lemma":"ōṭṭu","gloss":"drive away"},{"text":"இய","lemma":"iya","gloss":"past relative participle"}],"gloss":"who were driven away"},{"surface":"ஞான்றை","parts":[{"text":"ஞான்று","lemma":"ñāṉṟu","gloss":"time"},{"text":"ஐ","lemma":"ai","gloss":"oblique suffix"}],"gloss":"at the time of"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"தலைப்பெயர்த்து","parts":[{"text":"தலை","lemma":"talai","gloss":"head"},{"text":"பெயர்த்து","lemma":"peyarttu","gloss":"having turned"}],"gloss":"having turned back"},{"surface":"இட்ட","parts":[{"text":"இட்ட","lemma":"இட்ட","gloss":"dropped"}],"gloss":"dropped","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"வேலினும்","parts":[{"text":"வேல்","lemma":"vēl","gloss":"spear"},{"text":"இன்","lemma":"iṉ","gloss":"than"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"um","gloss":"even"}],"gloss":"even than the spears"},{"surface":"பலவே","parts":[{"text":"பல","lemma":"pala","gloss":"many"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ē","gloss":"indeed"}],"gloss":"are indeed more"}]}],"literal":"O Ay of the shining-gemmed curved ornaments! In your country, / does a young female elephant give birth to ten in a single pregnancy? / To those who come singing of you and your mountain, / without hiding your pleasant face, rejoicing, you gifted / majestic elephants. If counted, they are more than the spears / dropped by the Kongu warriors when they turned back and fled / as they were driven to the western sea.","translation":"O Ay, wearing curved ornaments set with shining gems! Does a young female elephant in your country give birth to ten calves in a single pregnancy? For, the majestic elephants you have joyfully gifted, with a welcoming face, to those who come singing of you and your mountain, are far more in number than the spears dropped by the Kongu warriors when they turned back and fled, driven all the way to the western sea!","modern":"விளங்கும் மணிகள் பதித்த வளைந்த அணிகலன்களை அணிந்த ஆய் மன்னனே! உன்னுடைய நாட்டில் உள்ள இளமையான பெண் யானை ஒரு பிரசவத்தில் பத்து குட்டிகளை ஈன்றெடுக்கிறதா? உன்னையும் உனது மலையையும் பாடி வரும் இரவலர்களுக்கு, உனது இன்முகத்தை மறைக்காமல் மகிழ்ச்சியோடு நீ பரிசாக வழங்கிய பெருமைமிக்க யானைகளின் எண்ணிக்கை, கொங்கு நாட்டு வீரர்கள் மேற்கு கடல் வரை விரட்டியடிக்கப்பட்டபோது, அவர்கள் பயந்து பின்வாங்கி ஓடி வழியில் போட்டுவிட்டுச் சென்ற வேல்களின் எண்ணிக்கையை விடவும் பல மடங்கு அதிகமானவை ஆகும்!","explanation":"The poet Uṟaiyūr Ēṇiccēri Muṭamōciyār addresses the chieftain Āy Aṇṭiraṉ in this poem of praise. He marvels at the chieftain's boundless generosity in gifting elephants to visiting bards. To express this, the poet uses a hyperbolic question, asking if the female elephants in Ay's country give birth to ten calves at once. He explains that the number of majestic elephants Ay has joyfully gifted to those who sing of him is greater than the countless spears dropped by the retreating Kongu warriors. These enemies had dropped their weapons in panic as Ay's forces chased them all the way to the western sea. The key words are 'piṭi' (female elephant), 'aḷitta' (gifted), and 'vēliṉum palavē' (more than the spears).","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"}}